device failed to flag a clinically significant ventricular tachycardia episode in real time, with confirmed recurrence across the deployed population (SYNTHETIC NARRATIVE). This represents a realized serious harm scenario due to the potential for severe patient consequences from missed arrhythmia detection. The confirmation of recurrence establishes a broad deployed-population impact and necessitates immediate field safety action.  The device's failure to perform as intended violates the requirements for electronic programmable systems outlined in MDR Annex I, Section 17.1 (mdr-annexI-sec17.1-electronic-programmable), which mandates repeatability, reliability, and performance aligned with intended use. Furthermore, this incident highlights a deficiency in the software development lifecycle, requiring adherence to state-of-the-art practices including risk management and verification/validation as stipulated by MDR Annex I, Section 17.2 (mdr-annexI-sec17.2-software-lifecycle). The device being automated with computer software triggers design control requirements under 21 CFR \u00a7 820.10(c) (qmsr-820.10-c-design-development), necessitating a review of the design and development process to prevent recurrence.  The device confidence-score logs for both missed events (ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A, ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A) provide direct evidence of the failure.", "recommendation": "ESCALATE_TO_HUMAN_IMMEDIATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 4}, "final_report_sha256": "bb71fad9bbb208af1738c098ece5d3782a786eda3ea596e5b6e052275b5f8bec", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["severity4_or_death_forced_immediate_human_escalation", "technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "ESCALATE_TO_HUMAN_IMMEDIATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0029", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 0, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0029_